## 2\. Requests, easiest first

### R1. Attire table: 129 -> 400 places (A3) — small, already tested in game

I patched these exact values into **svr2011.exe 1.0.1** and launched it on an "all attires" table (175 records, the
four mode tables merged): **it works in game in your recomp** (tested 2026-11-06). The same 400-place change is also
in a separate `defaultTENUES.xex` for Xenia.

Change in `port/tools/anthology\_redo.py` (same substitutions as today, bigger numbers):

```python
# A3: a table of 80 entries of 40 bytes (count at +3200) -> 400 entries (count at +16000)
('A3', 'sub\_828C40D0', \[('ctx.r3.s64 = 3204;', 'ctx.r3.s64 = 16004;', 1),
                        # (the other allocation path, in 16-byte units: 201 -> 1001, room for the 16004)
                        ('ctx.r3.s64 = 201;', 'ctx.r3.s64 = 1001;', 1)]),
('A3', 'sub\_828C3F28', \[('ctx.r9.s64 = 80;', 'ctx.r9.s64 = 400;', 1),
                        ('ctx.r3.u32 + 3200', 'ctx.r3.u32 + 16000', 1)]),
('A3', 'sub\_828C3F70', \[('ctx.r3.u32 + 3200', 'ctx.r3.u32 + 16000', 1)]),
('A3', 'sub\_828C3FF8', \[('ctx.r3.u32 + 3200', 'ctx.r3.u32 + 16000', 1)]),
('A3', 'sub\_828C4060', \[('ctx.r3.u32 + 3200', 'ctx.r3.u32 + 16000', 1)]),
('A3', 'sub\_828C4140', \[('ctx.r3.u32 + 3200', 'ctx.r3.u32 + 16000', 1)]),
('A3', 'sub\_828C4400', \[('ctx.r3.u32 + 3200', 'ctx.r3.u32 + 16000', 1),
                        ('ctx.r28.u32 + 3200', 'ctx.r28.u32 + 16000', 1)]),
```

Why it is safe: the loader `sub\_828C4400` copies as many 40-byte records as the file declares, **without any bound**,
so the table must only be at least as big as the file. Yumboy11's files have 129 records, so nothing changes for them;
modders get room for 271 more. (Same remark for vanilla 2011, where your D14 note lists "COS attire from misc.pac (80
records)" as a remaining limit.)

In the 1.0.1 binary, the ten compiled values were (RVA of the function, offset, 129-place value -> 400-place value):
`0x48DADF0` +0xA7 5164 -> 16004, +0xC6 323 -> 1001, +0x11A 129 -> 400, +0x133 5160 -> 16000, +0x15B 129 -> 400 (loop
counter, the r9 value compiled twice); `0x48DB300` +0x3, `0x48DB460` +0x41, `0x48DB600` +0x3, `0x48DB790` +0x4E,
`0x48DD840` +0x1E0: 5160 -> 16000 (file offset = RVA - 0xC00).

### R2. Bigger pac lists (`.h`) — small to medium

`CYFilePacListLoader` (same function in all four SvR games; Anthology guest `0x826B97F0`, SvR 2011 `0x826B902C`)
reserves **6 144 bytes** for the `.h` file and a table of **512 lines** (64-byte names). Yumboy11's lists are at
6 122-6 125 bytes, so a new character can no longer get its own `ch\\NNN.pac` (my tool now stores new attires inside an
existing pac, like Yumboy11 does for 37 superstars, but that is a workaround). A hook giving e.g. 32 KB / 2 048 lines
would remove this limit. Please also check the headroom of the pac directory memory (A1, 0x4B000 bytes) when more
pacs are mounted.

Gotcha if you ever mount Anthology from the pacs' own tables (your `PacListFolder` / `SVR2011\_TEST\_PLIST` path,
`sub\_825953B0`): it **crashes on Anthology** (I tried it on 1.0.1: "read of guest 0x30414000", lr in `sub\_826B87B0`,
r8 = 'EMD ', r7 = '0202'). Cause: 13 Anthology pacs have a TOC header that disagrees with `plist360.arc`:
`ch\\101.pac`, `ch\\102.pac`, `ch\\59.pac` count their EMD directory with 3 words too many (59/56, 51/48, 55/52; the .arc
is right), so the search walks 12 bytes past the end of `ch\\101.pac` and off the 0x4B000 directory memory; the others
have entries renamed only in the .arc (`MatchHD.pac`: 81 `/MENU/000L…` names, your A5; `evtgdhd.pac`,
`E4 / W0 / EC / ED.pac`, `dhb.pac`, `py2.pac`) or a different size (`menu.pac`, `ch\\241.pac`). The game itself only
reads the .arc, so Anthology is fine as shipped; but any feature that trusts the pacs' own TOCs needs the .arc
sections instead. Also: Yumboy11 numbers the .arc sections of lines 248-378 by **pac number**, not by line; the game
(`sub\_826B9350`) ignores that number (k-th non-empty section = line k), so tools must too.

### R3. More than 242 superstars in Anthology (your D14 route B / `big\_roster`) — big

This is the one that really adds slots. **A step-by-step plan with the exact functions (from the 2011 disc program
your build recompiles) is in `BIG\_ROSTER\_ANTHOLOGY\_PLAN.md`, with the full function map in
`big\_roster\_map\_svr2011.csv`.** Facts from Anthology that may help:

* Every index 0-241 is used (ids 50-69, 100-321 except 242), ids 70-99 are all used by DLC characters, the 137
`kPool` ids are all Yumboy11's. New characters therefore need **ids >= 322 and indices >= 292** (indices 242-291
are already the 50 CAWs in the index -> id table, which has 292 entries; tables: `u16\[322]` at `0x82DB3610`, its
reverse `u16\[292]` at `0x82DB3898`, the present table `u8\[322]` at `0x82DB3AE0`).
* Save: records 242 x 260 B and profiles 242 x 1 056 B at fixed offsets (your D14 note); a side file for the
extension (like your planned `00mods.dat`) would keep `SaveData.dat` compatible with Xenia, which matters to
Anthology players who move saves between the two.
* Per-id data that a new id needs (what my tool writes when it adds a character): `chEtc.pac` CHAR/DAT (264 B record)
and CHAR/PRO (profile: moveset, entrance block at +0x1C0), COS attire records, `ch\\NNN.pac` (or a host pac), renders
(SSFA / SSFB / SSFC, icon SSFD) by id, name text ids in `string.pac`, the announcer's name.
* Anthology also has 8 modes (8 xex, each with its own `.h` list; 4 different COS tables: `pac\\misc.pac`,
`pac\\07\\misc.pac`, `pac\\rr\\misc.pac`, `pac\\lm\\misc.pac`): an extension would have to work for every mode.

